#!/usr/bin/env python3
# QUARANTINED_R7_R1_ARCHIVE: historical source only; never execute or import.
"""Fresh-case runner for the isolated ``SIM_Bslosh_R1`` release.

This program deliberately has no dependency on the original
``SMPCC-SIM-40-64-88-v0.1`` campaign runner.  ``SIM_Bslosh_R1`` is a
simulation-only controller release, not a physical-alignment freeze:

* it has *cases* and *attempts*, never original-matrix planned rows;
* every live case starts one owned proxy environment on fresh ROS/Gazebo
  ports, and terminates only process groups it started;
* H_proxy (``/slosh/height``) and H_modal (``/sim_spmpc/slosh_height``) are the
  only liquid channels recorded.  No ``/sim_truth`` topic is accepted;
* the precise 60-second outcome window starts at first observed base motion,
  not at process launch; both success and timeout retain the same frozen tail;
* result and bag storage is the SIM-ONLY release namespace.  Passing the
  original protocol ID, an original matrix root, or a planned-row-looking
  identifier fails before ROS/Gazebo is launched.

The external proxy scripts under ``/data/a/scout_sim_replacement/scripts``
remain opaque subprocesses.  In particular, the historic SPMPC *attach*
wrapper is never used: it can launch a generic planner and therefore cannot
prove the dedicated R1 admission gate.  This runner starts the environment
wrapper only, then starts the fixed JSON path replayer and dedicated
``spmpc_sim_only_bslosh_r1.launch`` as separately owned children.

The public ``run`` command writes real case artifacts only under the storage
roots frozen by the SIM-ONLY release manifest.  ``--dry-run`` is useful for
testing the ledger/state machine; every such attempt is permanently labelled
``dry_run=true`` and ``SIMULATION_ONLY_NOT_PHYSICAL_PRIMARY``.
"""

from __future__ import annotations
raise SystemExit("QUARANTINED_R7_R1_ARCHIVE: this historical source is not executable")


